= Perception — Simple =

'''Perception''' is how the brain and body make sense of sensory information.

Your eyes receive light, but perception is what lets you experience shapes, objects, distance, motion, and faces.

Perception is not a perfect camera. The same sensory information can sometimes be understood in more than one way, and expectations or context can change what you notice.

[[Attention/Simple|Attention]] helps choose which information gets more processing.

Perceptual illusions are useful because they show the rules and assumptions the perceptual system normally uses.

